# BMW 7 Series E32 four-door saloon, 1987-1994.
#
# The first V8 and V12 7-series: 4,910 mm long, 1,845 mm wide, 1,411 mm high,
# 2,833 mm wheelbase (long-wheelbase 7,500iL 4,970/2,947); 3.0-5.0 sixes and
# V8/V12. The strongest-evidenced 1980s class-4 saloon in the section F research.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_7_Series_(E32)
#
# Colours: Diamond Black, Sterling Silver, Royal Blue and Oxford Green are
# documented BMW finishes of the period.
#
# Weight: 40 in total (black 15, silver 12, blue 8, green 5), below the Jaguar XJ's
# 60 and above the Mercedes W140's 20 to match the measured parc ratios.
#
# Speed 230 km/h; comfort 140/390 (line). Class 4.
# Dates: 1987-1994 with a road tail to about 2006.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-e32.blend. References:
# citycars/references/bmw-e32/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
